{
  "suite": "active_auth",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "description": "Active Authentication: the ActiveAuthenticationInfo friendly-name tables and the challenge-signature verifier. RSA cases walk the full ISO 9796-2-style recovery upstream implements: one per ISO 10118-3 trailer, plus the wrong-hash and unknown-trailer failures, the out-of-range signature, the small-modulus underflow (dart-only; upstream crashes), the empty-recovered-message boundary that pins the guard from below, and the leading-zero decrypt. ECDSA cases drive the plain r||s split and the lowercase-contains digest chain, including its SHA-256 default and the RIPEMD-160 always-fail. Keys and signatures are authored independently (Python/OpenSSL), not by the implementation under test.",
  "runners": [
    "dart",
    "swift"
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "aaInfo signature algorithm 0.4.0.127.0.7.1.1.4.1.1 -> ecdsa-plain-SHA1",
